  "worked_solution": "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all\u00a0}{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}={-2,-1}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}={-1,0}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={0,1}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=\u2205.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
